From: sliva0 <sliva0mk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Add QoS-Capability from RFC 5777
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

RFC 5777 defines this AVP in the IETF space, which the dictionary has no
entry for at its code:

  QoS-Capability (578): Grouped, 1 member, section 6

Each entry's type, enumerated values and grouped members are the
document's, from its clauses and AVP tables, and so are its M and V bits
where the document states them.

The document states no M bit for QoS-Capability: RFC 6733 section 4.1
leaves it to the application that uses an AVP, so its mandatory
attribute is left at the dictionary's default, and section 4.1.1 forbids
the V bit in the IETF space.

Generated by Seanchaí (integrations/wireshark/additions.py).
---
 resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
index 56a8586..fb25dd8 100644
--- a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
+++ b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
@@ -2742,6 +2742,11 @@
 				<gavp name="QoS-Parameters"/>
 			</grouped>
 		</avp>
+		<avp name="QoS-Capability" code="578" vendor-bit="mustnot">
+			<grouped>
+				<gavp name="QoS-Profile-Template"/>
+			</grouped>
+		</avp>
 
 		<!--
 		578 QoS-Capability [RFC5777]
